  "result_interpretation": "restored_fraction = 1.0000 (CI95=0.0000) for EVERY cell, both pair types, all 4 architectures, both seeds -- this is the EXPECTED sanity/wiring-check result (a full-state patch at the readout position trivially restores the clean logit regardless of which specific feature differed, since the readout state IS the entirety of what the recognition head sees -- mirrors cycle-navigation grammar_pairs's own rf~1.0 full-state result). It confirms the harness plumbing is correct for all 4 architectures on marked-reversal (a precondition for conditions 2/3) but cannot on its own attribute the effect to marker features specifically.\n\nThe mean_abs_clean_corrupt_logit_gap values ARE informative independent of the patch, and surface a notable, DECISIVE finding for marker_position_pairs specifically: rnn (both seeds, gap 0.0000-0.0005) and lstm seed10 (gap 0.0065) show a near-ZERO behavioral gap when the marker is moved far off-center while marker_count stays 1 -- i.e. RNN barely reacts at all to a marker-position violation alone. This is NOT a contradiction of Phase 2's marker_position_bin probe selectivity (~0.23-0.28, present for all architectures including rnn) -- it is the CAUSAL confirmation of the length_parity finding from the P4 revision: RNN's actual accept/reject mechanism checks marker_count and sequence-length parity, NOT marker centering. marker_position_pairs keeps length odd (101) and marker_count=1 in both clean and corrupt -- exactly the conditions under which the P3 layer-sweep found RNN's is_balanced_given_odd_length probe flat at 0.0000-0.0018 (no marker-centering signal). So RNN correctly (from a shortcut-detection standpoint) treats this corrupt example as CLEAN-like, producing a near-zero logit gap -- fully consistent with, not contradicting, the corrected P4 mechanism. lstm seed1, transformer (both seeds), and mamba (both seeds) show large gaps (0.64-8.76) on the same pair type, confirming those architectures DO use marker position (not just count) directly, matching their \"marker_count/marker_position, no length-parity refinement\" mechanism label in the corrected P4. lstm seed10 patterns with rnn here (near-zero gap) while lstm seed1 does not -- a seed-dependent LSTM result worth a closer look in a follow-up, but not one that changes the primary marker_count result, which is unambiguous: large logit gaps (5.2-10.3) for every architecture, every seed."
}